  [PASS] V2 the intrinsic remnant after the IMF side: the M/L lens is the LOOCV penalty; resolving it to ATLAS3D-class leaves 0.071 dex
         measured: intr_remnant = 0.0706 dex (17.66%) from sqrt(E1_loocv^2 - lens^2 + IMF^2) with lens = 0.0472 dex, IMF = 0.015 dex in v; E1(in) = 0.0713 dex; RAR floor = 0.045-0.052 dex
         reading : the truly-intrinsic bound after the IMF side = 0.0706 dex (17.7%), agreeing with G087's in-sample E1 (0.0713) to within 1% -- the M/L lens IS the non-generalizing systematics; but even fully resolved masses leave the scatter 1.4x ABOVE the RAR within-galaxy noise floor 0.045-0.052 dex: the pure-mass side of the BTFR does NOT reach the noise floor -- zero intrinsic scatter is NOT demonstrable from mass resolution alone.
  [PASS] V3 the honest statement: the resolved-mass era will pin the floor, not erase it -- THE NUMBER
         measured: sigma_v: 2026 = 0.1029 (26.74%); JWST = 0.0845 (21.49%); IMF-limited = 0.0849 (21.60%); perfect-mass floor = 0.0836 (21.23%, 0.334 dex in M_b); post-IMF intrinsic remnant = 0.0706 (17.66%)
         reading : THE STATEMENT: the zero-parameter law's scatter floor with PERFECT masses = E1_loocv = 0.0836 dex = 21.2% in v (0.334 dex in M_b) -- NOT zero.  The resolved-mass era (JWST + TRGB + ATLAS3D-class IMF) will achieve sigma_v = 0.0845 dex (21.5%) and pin the truly-intrinsic remnant at 0.0706-0.0836 dex (17.7%-21.2%): the 'zero intrinsic scatter' claim SURVIVES only as an upper bound, and the next discriminator is the RAR white-noise floor 0.045-0.052 dex (the remnant still sits 1.4x above it).

